# measured 2026-09-11, CI run 34576423237 (all four matrix jobs reported 24)
# invocation: dilithion-node --datadir=<tmp> --port=18555 --rpcport=18556 --connect=127.0.0.1:1 --relay-only
#
# WHY 17 AND NOT 24. The census includes the headers hash-worker pool, sized from
# hardware_concurrency but CLAMPED (headers_manager.cpp:3617-3623): 4 if detection
# fails, CAPPED AT 8. So hash workers are in [1,8] and the rest of the census is
# fixed. From an observed 24 the fixed part is at least 24-8 = 16, so the smallest
# census a HEALTHY node can print on any runner shape is 16+1 = 17.
#
# 17 is therefore a floor that cannot fail on a healthy tree, which is the property
# this leg has broken three times. It is deliberately loose: tighten it once a run
# has printed the runner core count (now reported beside the census) so the
# core-independent part can be pinned exactly. Tracked as the baseline-tightening
# follow-up; do NOT raise it to 24 from a single runner shape.
17
